Adam Borowski <kilobyte@mimuw.edu.pl> writes:

> I'm at least among the moderately experienced (8 ascensions), but I
> have yet to die to a wand of death.

In my current logfile I have:

 - 2 killed by a death ray (a valkyrie in quest and a samurai
   on DL 13)
 - 4 killed by a bolt of lightning
 - 3 killed by a magic missile
 - 1 killed by a blast of frost

 and

 - 1 killed by a touch of death. (polymorphed chameleon in rogue's
                                  quest) 

In addition, I remember one winter wolf cub that killed two of my
characters by blasting at them from a dark corridor, but that happened
in the previous logfile.

So, for me, deaths caused by lack of reflection outnumber the touch
of death cases at least 10 to 1 in recent games.

(I have a third death ray death but that one was a nasty accident
during spellcasting with a wizard that had both reflection and magic
resistance). 

> Every time one is generated and a monster capable of using it lays
> his hand on it, I already had magic resistance, reflection or, in
> one case, dodged it due to AC.

I suppose that you don't visit Fort Ludious often? Or alternatively,
you have learned that it is not a good place to visit without
reflection. I have the subjective impression that it is more likely
than not that at least one soldier in the Fort has a wand of death. 

> On the other hand, I've lost 5 characters to touch of death so far.

Apart from the case of a major lich teleporting next to you and
killing you on the same turn, there really isn't need to die from the
touch. The key is to keep the offending monster away from you. Scrolls
of earth are very useful in this respect. 

> Ki-rins and angels start appearing around levels 15 and 20 (got
> both).

That's a major bad luck. I have met an angel out of endgame only a
couple of times (and I have >70 ascensions, don't know exact number).
Ki-rin are also mightily rare, and I see one of them in perhaps one
ascension in five or so, if even then. I can remember only one case of
a ki-rin appearing before I had the amulet.

> Guaranteed spellcasters include the titan on Medusa's ruins and many of 
> quest nemeses (it was nice meeting one of the latter).

There's no need to let the titan get near you, and you can also bypass
him using a wand of digging, if necessary. Quest nemeses with touch of
death are a special case and you can postpone meeting them until you
have magic resistance.

